Local compact Qwen4exp selected-ID intersection over upstream pooled-cache
state and visibility filtering. Unsupported layouts retain upstream masking.
CPU fallback honors the intersection and unsupported accelerators decline it.
This replaces the private prefix, prepared-key-cache and selection machinery.
The upstream fused dense selection-mask path remains available only when
selected-key attention is disabled; its early return must not bypass the
accepted compact path or the graph-disabled selected-key control.

Upstream shared-cache row lists retain src[5]; selected-ID intersection uses
src[6]. Preserve both the causal/sequence dependency and scalar CPU fallback
across upstream's mask-independent QSA selection.

Use total query tokens when shaping the fallback mask: its query dimension
may already be split by stream. Preserve already-canonical tensors by pointer:
per-layer identity views of the shared host mask otherwise become distinct
full-cache backend copies. Reshape only a genuinely different stream layout.

